00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.800
Today you will see history in the making.&nbsp;
Yes, we are going to have a look at AlphaFold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:15.920
from DeepMind, perhaps one of the most&nbsp;
important papers of the last few years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:23.440
This is a true gift to humanity. And, if&nbsp;
even that is not good enough, it gets better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:30.240
because today you will see how this&nbsp;
gift has now become 200 times bigger.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:38.000
So, what is AlphaFold? AlphaFold is an AI that is&nbsp;
capable of solving protein structure prediction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.640
which we will refer to as protein folding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.640
Okay…but what is a protein&nbsp;
and why does it need folding?

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:53.840
A protein is a string of amino acids, these are&nbsp;
the building blocks of life. This is what goes in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:03.600
which in reality, has a 3D structure. And that is&nbsp;
protein folding. Letters go in, a 3D object comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:11.600
out. This is hard. Really hard. For instance,&nbsp;
DeepMind’s earlier AI programs were able to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:20.080
hard games like Chess, Go, and Starcraft 2, and&nbsp;
none of these AIs were a match to protein folding.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.520
Yet, it has become the world’s&nbsp;
best solution at the CASP event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:31.760
I’ve heard DeepMind CEO Demis Hassabis&nbsp;
call it the Olympics of protein folding.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.840
If you look at how teams of scientists prepare&nbsp;
for this event, you will probably agree that yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.960
this is indeed the Olympics of protein folding.&nbsp;
And what is even more incredible is that it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:53.520
reached a score of 90, which means two amazing&nbsp;
things. One, in absolute terms, AlphaFold 2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.960
is considered to be about three times better than&nbsp;
previous solutions. And, it gets even better, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:06.720
score of 90 means that we can consider protein&nbsp;
folding as a mostly solved problem. Wow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.240
This is not something that I thought&nbsp;
I would be able to say in my lifetime.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.840
Now, we said that this is a&nbsp;
gift to humanity. Why is that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.200
Where is the gift part here?&nbsp;
What makes this a gift?

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:28.080
Well, a little after publishing the paper,&nbsp;
DeepMind made these 3D structure predictions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.320
available for free for everyone. For instance,&nbsp;
they have made their human protein predictions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.520
public. Beyond that, they already have&nbsp;
made their predictions public for yeast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.040
important pathogens, crop species, and more.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:49.040
I also said that AlphaFold 2 is not the&nbsp;
end, but a start of something great.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:56.640
I promised to tell you how it improves over&nbsp;
time, so here are two incredible revelations.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:04.240
One, we noted that AlphaFold will likely help&nbsp;
us fight diseases and develop new vaccines. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:11.120
hold on to your papers, because this is not&nbsp;
just talk, this is now a reality today: look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:17.600
this group was already able to accelerate their&nbsp;
research work a great deal due to AlphaFold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:24.560
in fighting antibiotic resistant bacteria. They&nbsp;
are studying how to fight deadly bacteria that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:31.360
modify their own membrane structure so that&nbsp;
the antibiotic can’t get in. That is a hugely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:37.520
important project for all of us. They noted that&nbsp;
they have been working vigorously on this project&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:43.760
for 10 years, and now that they have access&nbsp;
to AlphaFold, they could get a prediction done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:51.840
in 30 minutes, and this is something that was not&nbsp;
possible to do for 10 years before that. That is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:59.040
absolutely incredible. This is history in&nbsp;
the making. I love to be able to live through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:05.280
times like this. So thank you so much&nbsp;
for sharing this amazing moment with me.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.040
So this was one project, and what is this here?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.080
Oh yes, these are some more&nbsp;
of these AlphaFold predictions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:20.960
